":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":515.1018676757812,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":55.56904602050781,"r":290.7389221191406,"t":681.9437561035156},"charspan":[0,0],"page_no":1}],"references":[],"self_ref":"#/tables/0"}],"texts":[{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_header","orig":"MATEC Web of Conferences 148 , 05003 (2018) ICoEV 2017","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":787.7310847083178,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":46.0471,"r":223.0216,"t":806.9201146484374},"charspan":[0,54],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"MATEC Web of Conferences 148 , 05003 (2018) ICoEV 2017"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_header","orig":"https://doi.org/10.1051/matecconf/201814805003","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":799.3897404836268,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":373.1956,"r":552.0346000000001,"t":806.7941146484375},"charspan":[0,46],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"https://doi.org/10.1051/matecconf/201814805003"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"This can be explained by the relative high damping in the suspension of the coil (see Figure 5) combined with the relative small force introduced into the shaker by the impact hammer, leading to a totally damped acceleration response of the table.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":711.3304785213272,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.64095999999989,"r":288.7388399999999,"t":768.2132946484375},"charspan":[0,247],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"This can be explained by the relative high damping in the suspension of the coil (see Figure 5) combined with the relative small force introduced into the shaker by the impact hammer, leading to a totally damped acceleration response of the table."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Table 2. Modal parameters","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":690.672314686899,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":118.58,"r":226.82876,"t":699.6120946484375},"charspan":[0,25],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"Table 2. Modal parameters"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"4 Determination of the electrical parameters","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":458.1463451003039,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.63999999999999,"r":289.4160000000001,"t":483.7118146484375},"charspan":[0,44],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"4 Determination of the electrical parameters"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Looking at (1) gives us the needed electrical parameters to  be  defined.  We  find R and L ,  the  resistance  and  the inductance of the coil, µf ,  the  force  constant,  and µbemf , the  bemf  (back  electromagnetic  force)  constant  of  the system.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":390.63919468689903,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.629879999999986,"r":288.73940000000005,"t":447.9435346484375},"charspan":[0,254],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"Looking at (1) gives us the needed electrical parameters to  be  defined.  We  find R and L ,  the  resistance  and  the inductance of the coil, µf ,  the  force  constant,  and µbemf , the  bemf  (back  electromagnetic  force)  constant  of  the system."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"R and L are  the  intrinsic  electrical  properties  of  the coil and  are  purely  passive.  A  simple  measurement  on the RLC meter will allow us to get those values. These are given in Table 3.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":342.373034686899,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.65147999999999,"r":288.5202800000001,"t":387.5871346484375},"charspan":[0,197],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"R and L are  the  intrinsic  electrical  properties  of  the coil and  are  purely  passive.  A  simple  measurement  on the RLC meter will allow us to get those values. These are given in Table 3."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The quantities µf and µbemf are  representative  of  the same phenomenon - the expression of the Lorentz force - but have neither the same causes nor the same effects.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":306.13919468689903,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.630839999999964,"r":288.59924,"t":339.2120546484375},"charspan":[0,167],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"The quantities µf and µbemf are  representative  of  the same phenomenon - the expression of the Lorentz force - but have neither the same causes nor the same effects."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Lorentz expresses that the charge carriers of a conductor immersed in a (non-collinear) magnetic field are subjected to a force when moving and this according to the following relation:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":257.773434686899,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.62087999999994,"r":284.44591999999994,"t":302.9576546484375},"charspan":[0,185],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"Lorentz expresses that the charge carriers of a conductor immersed in a (non-collinear) magnetic field are subjected to a force when moving and this according to the following relation:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"    B v q E Fq    (7)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":235.020071669333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":120.58986879999995,"r":288.74024000000003,"t":248.8004473484375},"charspan":[0,28],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"With Fq the  force  exerted  on  a  charge  carrier  of electrical  charge q subjected  to  an  electric  field E , undergoing a speed v , and immersed in a magnetic field B .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":176.950666965153,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.63623999999996,"r":288.73412,"t":222.09649464843756},"charspan":[0,175],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"With Fq the  force  exerted  on  a  charge  carrier  of electrical  charge q subjected  to  an  electric  field E , undergoing a speed v , and immersed in a magnetic field B ."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The generalized expression of this force on a conductor of length l is:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":152.70802696515307,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.63623999999995,"r":288.5149999999998,"t":173.80597464843754},"charspan":[0,71],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/11","text":"The generalized expression of this force on a conductor of length l is:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"i Bli F f   (8)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":129.19270761911207,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":127.81420299999998,"r":288.74516,"t":141.17209464843745},"charspan":[0,18],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/12","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The current i flowing in the coil generates a force F on the latter with respect to the force constant µf .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":94.40423904726447,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.63731999999993,"r":288.73918399999997,"t":115.74421464843749},"charspan":[0,107],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/13","text":"The current i flowing in the coil generates a force F on the latter with respect to the force constant µf ."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The  magnitude µbemf expresses  the  force  undergone by  the  electrons  in  a  conductor  which  moves  in  a magnetic field. The displacement of the coil generates an electric potential at the conductor terminals with respect to the bemf constant.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":58.55319468689902,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.64716,"r":288.56575999999995,"t":91.6242546484375},"charspan":[0,169],"page_no":1},{"bbox":{"b":747.566074686899,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.05348000000004,"r":540.8426000000006,"t":768.5076546484376},"charspan":[170,250],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/14","text":"The  magnitude µbemf expresses  the  force  undergone by  the  electrons  in  a  conductor  which  moves  in  a magnetic field. The displacement of the coil generates an electric potential at the conductor terminals with respect to the bemf constant."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"We study a system which on the one hand generates a force due to an applied current and on the other hand which creates an electrical potential with respect to the speed of the  coil .  This  approach  forms  the  basis  of  the development  of  a  two-port  network  model  and  goes beyond the scope of this work. Different authors such as York,  Smallwood  or  Guillaume  develop  this  aspect deeper in detail [11-13].","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":650.9341546868991,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.0435200000001,"r":541.1015600000004,"t":744.3646146484375},"charspan":[0,422],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/15","text":"We study a system which on the one hand generates a force due to an applied current and on the other hand which creates an electrical potential with respect to the speed of the  coil .  This  approach  forms  the  basis  of  the development  of  a  two-port  network  model  and  goes beyond the scope of this work. Different authors such as York,  Smallwood  or  Guillaume  develop  this  aspect deeper in detail [11-13]."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"4.1 Experimental  determination  of  the  force constant","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":609.7705949234867,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.05348000000015,"r":541.1583320000004,"t":631.0596546484376},"charspan":[0,56],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/16","text":"4.1 Experimental  determination  of  the  force constant"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"First, we used the assembly already presented in Figure 3 which blocks the vibrating table. A voltage is applied to the terminals which generates a current, which creates a force.  Due to the rigid structure, the table cannot  move and no bemf can settle.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":541.9319146868991,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.05348000000004,"r":541.1513600000001,"t":599.2673346484376},"charspan":[0,255],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/17","text":"First, we used the assembly already presented in Figure 3 which blocks the vibrating table. A voltage is applied to the terminals which generates a current, which creates a force.  Due to the rigid structure, the table cannot  move and no bemf can settle."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"A  measurement  of  the  force  with  respect  to  the current yields the force constant. The latter is shown in Figure 9 for three different drive voltages.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":505.80699468689915,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.05348000000004,"r":540.9521600000004,"t":538.8698946484376},"charspan":[0,157],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/18","text":"A  measurement  of  the  force  with  respect  to  the current yields the force constant. The latter is shown in Figure 9 for three different drive voltages."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"We  immediately notice a very strong structural response at 660 Hz due to the resonance of the structure originally  intended  to  be  rigid.  By  performing  a  modal analysis  of  this  structure,  we  obtained  its  frequency response. The synthesized curve has been superimposed on the measured curves to emphasize the response due to the resonance of the beam structure.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":421.196794686899,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.0534800000001,"r":540.9521600000007,"t":502.6254546484376},"charspan":[0,375],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/19","text":"We  immediately notice a very strong structural response at 660 Hz due to the resonance of the structure originally  intended  to  be  rigid.  By  performing  a  modal analysis  of  this  structure,  we  obtained  its  frequency response. The synthesized curve has been superimposed on the measured curves to emphasize the response due to the resonance of the beam structure."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Fig. 9. Force Constant analysis for different drive voltages. The synthesized FRF of the beam structure is superimposed on the measured curves to emphasize the response due to the resonance of the beam structure.","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":215.3787002253606,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.05,"r":540.9116,"t":255.85681464843753},"charspan":[0,212],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/20","text":"Fig. 9. Force Constant analysis for different drive voltages. The synthesized FRF of the beam structure is superimposed on the measured curves to emphasize the response due to the resonance of the beam structure."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Force Constant","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":402.8900146484375,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":411.3333333333333,"r":443.33333333333337,"t":408.2233479817708},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/21","text":"Force Constant"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"1","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":316.22334798177087,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":320.6666666666667,"r":325.3333333333333,"t":336.2233479817708},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/22","text":"1"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Dnve Voltage 0 5V","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":295.22334798177087,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":442.66666666666663,"r":478.0,"t":301.55668131510413},"charspan":[0,17],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/23","text":"Dnve Voltage 0 5V"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Dnve Voltage IV","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":290.22334798177087,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":442.66666666666663,"r":474.66666666666663,"t":296.55668131510413},"charspan":[0,15],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/24","text":"Dnve Voltage IV"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Frequency (Hz)","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":270.55668131510413,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":412.3333333333333,"r":440.66666666666663,"t":276.55668131510413},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/25","text":"Frequency (Hz)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Beyond  this,  the  measurements  tend  to  show  an increase in damping with the drive voltage underlying a possible non-linearity of the system.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":170.62931468689908,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.04688,"r":540.8967560000001,"t":203.72209464843752},"charspan":[0,146],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/26","text":"Beyond  this,  the  measurements  tend  to  show  an increase in damping with the drive voltage underlying a possible non-linearity of the system."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"At this point any deduction is dangerous and should be avoided. Further analysis is required. Nevertheless, in the area below 100 Hz, the relative theoretical error due to the resonating structure with respect to the unity does not exceed 3%. Despite a relative variation in amplitude of 5% over the frequencies, the value of µf is considered to  be  constant.  Its  average  value  is  7.8493  N/A  against an initial value form the manufacturer of 6.4 N/A. These data are shown in Table 3.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":61.91783468689903,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.03692000000007,"r":541.1049200000002,"t":167.44777464843753},"charspan":[0,491],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/27","text":"At this point any deduction is dangerous and should be avoided. Further analysis is required. Nevertheless, in the area below 100 Hz, the relative theoretical error due to the resonating structure with respect to the unity does not exceed 3%. Despite a relative variation in amplitude of 5% over the frequencies, the value of µf is considered to  be  constant.  Its  average  value  is  7.8493  N/A  against an initial value form the manufacturer of 6.4 N/A. These data are shown in Table 3."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"5","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":14.383932243092318,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":297.2638,"r":302.2638,"t":22.611014648437504},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/28","text":"5"}],"version":"1.10.0"}